File: mnemon

File format: File mnemon is used by both asem7.cpp and pep7.cpp. The
first three lines are input during initialization of both programs. All
text after the first three lines is ignored. The first three lines contain
the mnemonics of the unimplemented op-codes and can be changed by the
user to work the problems from Chapter 8 of "Computer Systems".

Line format: If the first character is not 'u' or 'U' the instruction is
not a unary instruction. The second character is skipped. The third
character is the first letter of the mnemonic. Each character is converted
to uppercase, so that HEXo is stored as HEXO. The mnemonic terminates with
the space character ' ' and can be no longer than eight characters. The
last group is a string of up to four lowercase characters with no trailing
spaces that indicate the allowable addressing modes for the instruction.
The letters can be in any order.
